[size=5][b]Mojave Desktop Radio[/b][/size]
[i]Your Spotify, on the Pip-Boy.[/i]

Adds the radio station [b]Mojave Desktop Radio[/b] to the Pip-Boy. Tune in and the [b]Spotify desktop app[/b] on your PC starts playing. Pause, skip and see the current artist and title right on the Radio tab - and, if you like, make it sound like a 50s radio.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]A real Pip-Boy station: tune in / out like Radio New Vegas. Spotify pauses (or mutes) when you switch to another station - the game radio and Spotify never play at the same time.
[*]Pip-Boy panel with [b]PAUSE / NEXT TRACK / PREVIOUS TRACK / CHANGE FX MODE[/b], live artist, title and status.
[*]Four sound presets: [b]Clean[/b], [b]Mojave Radio[/b] (old speaker), [b]Wasteland Radio[/b] (mono, hiss, crackle, tuning sweep), [b]Damaged Radio[/b] (weak signal, fading, dropouts - still listenable). Fully adjustable in MCM.
[*]Smooth 150-350 ms fades when tuning in and out.
[*]Corner message on track change. All Pip-Boy texts translatable in an INI.
[*]No keys bound by default. Optional hotkeys in MCM.
[*]Only Spotify is ever controlled - never YouTube, other players or your keyboard media keys.
[*][i]Optional:[/i] control foobar2000, MusicBee, AIMP or WACUP / Winamp instead (MCM > Desktop Player). Not tested by me - the player must show up in the Windows media controls. Spotify users don't need to change anything.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Safe for your game[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Tiny ESP (3 records) that [b]overrides nothing[/b] - add it to or remove it from any save.
[*]No vanilla or UI-mod file replaced: the Pip-Boy panel is injected with UIO (works with Vanilla UI Plus, yUI, Pip-Boy 2000 Mk VI).
[*]No new script commands (no opcode conflicts possible). The plugin never blocks the game: if the desktop part is closed or crashes, the station simply shows SIGNAL LOST.
[*]Nothing is written to Overwrite. No audio is ever saved to disk.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Fallout: New Vegas 1.4.0.525 (Steam / GOG)
[*][url=https://github.com/xNVSE/NVSE/releases]xNVSE[/url] 6.3+
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/newvegas/mods/58277]JIP LN NVSE[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/newvegas/mods/72541]ShowOff xNVSE[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/newvegas/mods/57174]UIO - User Interface Organizer[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/newvegas/mods/42507]The Mod Configuration Menu[/url] + [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/newvegas/mods/93642]MCM Extender[/url] (for the settings page)
[*][url=https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/8.0].NET 8 Desktop Runtime x64[/url]
[*]Windows 10 21H2+ or Windows 11, Spotify desktop app
[*]For the sound effects (optional): [url=https://vb-audio.com/Cable/]VB-CABLE[/url] (free) or Steam Streaming Speakers (comes with Steam)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install with MO2 / Vortex (or extract into Data). Enable [b]MojaveDesktopRadio.esp[/b] - load order does not matter.
[*]Open Spotify and play any song once.
[*]Start the game with NVSE and load a save. A small tray app (green radio icon) starts by itself and closes with the game.
[*]Pip-Boy > DATA > RADIO > [b]Mojave Desktop Radio[/b].
[/list]

[size=4][b]How the sound effect works[/b][/size]
While the station is tuned, Spotify's output is moved to a virtual device nobody hears, the companion app applies the preset in real time and plays it on your normal speakers. Fallout's own sound never goes through it. When you leave the station or quit the game, Spotify is put back to its normal device - even after a crash. Without a virtual device everything works, just without the effect.

[size=4][b]About Spotify[/b][/size]
The mod uses no Spotify servers, API or account data, and records nothing. Control goes through Windows' media controls (like your keyboard media keys); the effect processes what your PC is already playing, like an equalizer. The [i]Clean[/i] preset leaves the sound untouched.

[size=4][b]Known limits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Gamepads cannot select the panel entries - use the MCM hotkeys.
[*]Spotify must have played once since it started (it registers with Windows on first playback).
[*]Other players (optional) work only if they publish Windows media controls - check with [i]mdr.exe players[/i] (see README).
[*]Tale of Two Wastelands and DarNified UI are not tested.
[*]Do not merge the ESP into a merged patch.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Problems?[/b][/size]
Read [b]Docs\TROUBLESHOOTING.md[/b] in the archive. When reporting a bug, attach [i]MojaveDesktopRadio.log[/i] (game folder), [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\MojaveDesktopRadio\logs\bridgehost.log[/i] and [i]nvse.log[/i].

